WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.149
So nickel is a metal which can produce allergies
in some

00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:14.450
people, people get allergic to nickel. And
it’s a metal which is

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:20.460
found in Canada and Sir Ludwig Mond founder
of the

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:27.009
company that later becomes ICI discovered
a process for

00:00:27.009 --> 00:00:34.149
extracting nickel from the ore using carbon
monoxide and

00:00:34.149 --> 00:00:42.210
started a huge factory on the south coast
of Wales. And the

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.239
so-called nickel carbonyl was really quite
an important

00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:49.710
industrial compound even though it was fantastically
toxic.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:53.670
And it’s unusual as a metal compound because
it boils at

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:57.469
room temperature and usually one thinks of
metal

00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:01.690
compounds as salts. Nickel is now used quite
a lot in the

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:10.190
plating industry for plating materials, iron
and steel in

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:13.150
particular, and then often you would put chromium
or

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:17.470
something on top. Used to be used for plating
the inside of

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:22.520
tins for peas and things like that. And sometimes
the sulphur

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:28.110
from inside the peas would be released by
bacteria and would

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:31.520
react to find strange black spots across the
insides of the tin.

